COPY public.ai_analysis_results (id, ticker, analysis_text, generated_date) FROM stdin;
1	MRVL	| Metric | Value & Comments |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Current Price** | $203.015 |\n| **Trend** | Bullish |\n| **Support** | $190.85 (EMA10 dynamic support) |\n| **Resistance** | $205.00 (Psychological level / potential short-term high) |\n| **Entry** | $205.50 (Breakout confirmation above $205 psychological resistance) |\n| **Stop Loss** | $189.50 (Below EMA10 dynamic support) |\n| **Target** | $229.50 (1.5x Risk-to-Reward extension from entry) |\n| **Risk** | $16.00 |\n| **Reward** | $24.00 |\n| **RR** | 1.50 |\n| **Suggested Position Size** | AccountRisk / $16.00 |\n| **Trade Type** | Long |\n| **Confidence** | 75/100 |\n\n### Reasoning\nMRVL is in a strong bullish trend, with the current price significantly above its EMA10 ($190.85) and EMA20 ($179.19), which are both trending upwards and in bullish alignment. MACD (15.50) is above its signal line (14.35), indicating strong bullish momentum. Relative Volume (1.64) is above average, suggesting strong buying interest.\n\nHowever, the RSI (14) at 71.05 indicates the stock is currently overbought, which warrants caution as it could signal a potential short-term pullback. To mitigate this risk while capitalizing on the strong trend, a long entry is suggested only upon a confirmed breakout above the psychological resistance level of $205.00. An entry at $205.50 would confirm continued upside momentum despite the overbought RSI reading.\n\nThe Stop Loss is strategically placed below the EMA10 dynamic support at $189.50, allowing for a reasonable buffer. The Take Profit target of $229.50 is set to achieve a minimum Risk-to-Reward ratio of 1.5, projecting an extension of the current bullish move into new price territory. The setup carries a decent 75/100 confidence score, acknowledging the strong trend and confirmed momentum, but also the inherent risk of trading an overbought asset that requires a breakout for validation.	2026-05-29
2	NUE	| Metric | Value & Comments |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Current Price** | $249.83 |\n| **Trend** | Bullish |\n| **Nearest Support** | $235.95 (EMA10 dynamic support) |\n| **Nearest Resistance** | $250.00 (Psychological level, immediate resistance) |\n| **Suggested Entry Price** | $250.50 (Breakout confirmation above $250 psychological level) |\n| **Stop Loss** | $234.90 (Below EMA10 dynamic support) |\n| **Take Profit Target** | $275.00 (Based on projected resistance extension and favorable R:R) |\n| **Risk Per Share** | $15.60 |\n| **Reward Per Share** | $24.50 |\n| **Risk-to-Reward Ratio** | 1.57 |\n| **Position Size Formula** | AccountRisk / $15.60 |\n| **Breakout Confirmation Level** | $250.00 (Clearance of psychological resistance) |\n| **Confidence Score** | 65/100 |\n\n### Reasoning\nNUE is currently in a strong bullish trend, with the price trading significantly above its EMA10, EMA20, and SMA50. The MACD is above its signal line, confirming positive momentum. However, the Relative Strength Index (RSI) is at 73.26, indicating the stock is in overbought territory, which suggests caution for a direct entry. The current price is also approaching the psychological resistance level of $250.00.\n\nGiven the overbought conditions and proximity to resistance, a long entry is suggested only upon a confirmed breakout above $250.00. The entry price is set at $250.50 to validate this breakout. A stop loss is strategically placed below the EMA10 dynamic support at $234.90, defining a clear risk. The take profit target of $275.00 aims for a reasonable extension post-breakout, providing a favorable risk-to-reward ratio of 1.57, which meets the minimum requirement. The relative volume is below average (0.60), which could temper the strength of a breakout, contributing to a moderate confidence score.	2026-05-29
3	SMH	| Metric | Value & Comments |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Current Price** | $599.83 |\n| **Trend** | Bullish (Price above all EMAs/SMAs, MACD bullish, strong RSI) |\n| **Support** | $577.05 (EMA10) |\n| **Resistance** | $600.00 (Psychological level / Recent high) |\n| **Entry** | $600.10 (Breakout above psychological $600 level) |\n| **Stop Loss** | $575.00 (Below EMA10 support) |\n| **Target** | $637.75 (Projected resistance extension for 1.5 RR) |\n| **Risk** | $25.10 |\n| **Reward** | $37.65 |\n| **RR** | 1.50 |\n| **Suggested Position Size** | AccountRisk / $25.10 |\n| **Trade Type** | Long |\n| **Confidence** | 75/100 |\n\n### Reasoning\nSMH is currently in a strong bullish trend, with the current price trading significantly above its key moving averages (EMA10, EMA20, SMA50). The MACD shows bullish momentum as it is above its signal line, and the RSI (67.37) indicates strong buying pressure without yet being in overbought territory. The immediate psychological resistance level is at $600.00.\n\nA long trade setup is suggested based on a breakout above this $600.00 resistance. An entry at $600.10 confirms this breakout, aiming to capture further upward momentum. The stop loss is strategically placed below the EMA10 at $575.00, providing a buffer beneath the first dynamic support while keeping the risk manageable at 4.18% of the entry price. The take profit target at $637.75 is set to achieve a favorable risk-to-reward ratio of 1.50, projecting further price discovery beyond the recent high. While the relative volume is slightly below average (0.75), the overall technical picture supports a high-probability bullish continuation.	2026-05-29
4	QQQ	| Metric | Value & Comments |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Current Price** | $739.06 |\n| **Trend** | Bullish |\n| **Support** | $722.60 (EMA10) |\n| **Resistance** | $740.00 (Immediate psychological level / prior high) |\n| **Entry** | $740.50 (Breakout above immediate resistance) |\n| **Stop Loss** | $720.00 (Below EMA10 dynamic support) |\n| **Target** | $771.50 (Projected 1.5x Risk-to-Reward) |\n| **Risk** | $20.50 |\n| **Reward** | $31.00 |\n| **RR** | 1.51 |\n| **Suggested Position Size** | AccountRisk / $20.50 |\n| **Trade Type** | Long |\n| **Confidence** | 70/100 |\n\n### Reasoning\nQQQ is in a strong bullish trend, with the current price trading above EMA10 ($722.60), EMA20 ($706.93), and SMA50 ($652.92). The RSI (67.81) indicates strong momentum without being overbought, while the MACD (21.57) is above its signal line (21.51), confirming bullish momentum. Although relative volume is below average (0.49), the overall trend and momentum are favorable for a long position.\n\nWe are suggesting a breakout entry at $740.50, which is just above the immediate psychological resistance level of $740.00. This entry confirms sustained upward momentum beyond current price levels. The stop loss is placed strategically below the EMA10 support at $720.00, providing a buffer for volatility while staying within acceptable risk parameters (2.77% from entry). The target of $771.50 is set to achieve a favorable risk-to-reward ratio of 1.51, validating the trade setup. The confidence score is 70/100, reflecting the strong trend and momentum, though slightly tempered by the lower relative volume and the stock being in price discovery mode without explicit historical resistance levels.	2026-05-29
